<title>USA: Transportacion Ferroviara says finishes financing.</title>
<headline>Transportacion Ferroviara says finishes financing.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transportacion Ferroviara Mexicana said Monday it completed financing for its purchase of the Northeast Railroad concession from the Mexican government.</p>
<p>Transportacion Ferroviara is a joint venture between Kansas City Southern Industries Inc and Mexico's Transportacion Maritima Mexicana.</p>
<p>The company said it put in place $807 million of equity capital for the railroad and raised $725 million in debt financing. It said it also established bank revolving lines of credit of $150 million.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
</text>
